## T113 Deliverable: Collapse Toggle Suggestion

**Created:** S003 - "Conditional collapse toggle - show only when content overflows"

### Analysis

**Current Behavior:**
- Toggle shows when `content.length > 400 || lineCount > 8` (arbitrary thresholds)
- "Click to expand" hint appears regardless of actual visual overflow

**Problem:**
Messages meeting the threshold but fitting within `max-height: 12em` still show the toggle, which is misleading and clutters the UI.

**Recommendation:**
Check actual DOM overflow post-render instead of character/line counts:

```javascript
// After rendering content
requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    if (contentEl.scrollHeight > contentEl.clientHeight) {
        contentEl.classList.add('collapsible');
        // Add hint
    }
});
```

**Files Affected:** `studio-ui.js`, `studio.js`

