Got it - you want the **raw text** we inject, not just token counts. The text itself IS the data.

**Updated Task Data Schema:**
```
{
  "task_id": "T114",
  "name": "Fix suggestions system",
  "agent": "Programmer",

  "input": {
    "role_md": "# Programmer\n...",        // actual role.md content
    "skills": "## File Operations\n...",   // actual injected skills
    "task_prompt": "[WHAT] Fix..."         // actual task description
  },

  "execution": {
    "steps": 5,
    "errors": [],
    "duration_seconds": 45
  },

  "output": {
    "response": "## T114 Deliverable...",  // actual agent output
  },

  "cost": {
    "input_tokens": 2150,
    "output_tokens": 500
  }
}
```

This gives you full transparency - you can see exactly what went in and what came out.

